5. Read `.cursor/rules/unity-project.mdc` for project-specific constraints

## Unity MCP Tool Groups (Token Optimization)
Use `manage_tools list_groups` to see all groups, then activate only what you need:
- **core** (default) - GameObjects, scenes, assets, components, editor, camera, physics, packages, graphics, build
- **scripting_ext** - Execute code, scriptable objects (activate when writing scripts)
- **ui** - UI Toolkit (activate when editing UI)
- **animation** - Animation tools (activate when working on animations)
- **vfx** - VFX, particles, shaders, textures (activate when needed)
- **testing** - Test runner (activate for tests)
- **profiling** - Profiler (activate for optimization)
- **docs** - Unity docs (activate for documentation lookups)
- **probuilder** - ProBuilder (activate for level geometry)

## Code Standards
- No namespaces (global namespace only)
- PascalCase classes and filenames (must match)
- No spaces in file/folder names
- Singletons: `public static ClassName Instance` in Awake
- Async Task + CancellationTokenSource for UGS calls

## Token Optimization
- Query the graph first instead of reading large files
- Never read >400 line files fully unless necessary
- Grep first, read targeted methods second
- Batch independent reads in parallel
- Use `manage_tools deactivate` on unused groups to save tools list tokens
